    "url": "https://note.com/candicenina_enjp/n/nf9f34d7be529?hl=en",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "There are many consultation offices at universities. While 'mado' means 'window' in English, 'madoguchi' cannot be translated literally. (In the context of 'procedures,' the word 'window' refers to a 'time slot' or 'grace period.')",
    "url": "https://note.com/candicenina_enjp/n/nf9f34d7be529?hl=en",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Since 'madoguchi' are not as common in English-speaking countries as they are in Japan, it is more natural in English to",
    "url": "https://note.com/candicenina_enjp/n/nf9f34d7be529?hl=en",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "specify the name of the department or its role",
    "url": "https://note.com/candicenina_enjp/n/nf9f34d7be529?hl=en",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "rather than using the concept of a 'madoguchi.' Unless you specifically want to emphasize a 'reception counter,' it is wise to avoid literal translations like 'window' or 'counter.'",
    "url": "https://note.com/candicenina_enjp/n/nf9f34d7be529?hl=en",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
